                <head>96. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The Ministerial Council of the Organization for Economic Cooperation and
                    Development met in Paris December 2–3, 1964. Under Secretary of State George W. Ball headed the U.S. Delegation. A
                    summary of the OECD Ministerial proceedings is
                    in two parts, CEDTO A–386 from Paris, December
                    11, and CEDTO A–392 from Paris, December 11,
                    both in Department of State, Central Files, ECIN 3 OECD. For text of the December 3 communiqué, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">see American Foreign Policy: Current Documents</hi>,
                    1964, pages 497–499.</p>
                <p>Background and talking points papers on U.S. preparations for and participation
                    in the OECD Ministerial Council meeting are in
                    the Washington National Records Center, RG 286, DAC Material: FRC 70 A 5922,
                        Meetings—OECD Ministerial Dec. 2–3, 1964,
                    and Department of State, Conference Files: Lot 66 D 110, CF 2456–2457.</p>
            </div>
